openmediavault-filemanager (8.0) stable; urgency=low

  * Initial release: native file manager built on the declarative
    workbench framework.
  * Browse shared folders as list or tree, with the current location in
    the breadcrumb, and search recursively by name. Click a folder name
    to open it and a file name to open it in a new browser tab.
  * Create folders and files, rename, copy and move (also between shared
    folders), duplicate, create relative symbolic links, change
    permissions and owner.
  * Edit text files with a size limit; files are saved atomically, and
    not at all if they were changed by someone else in the meantime.
  * Calculate MD5/SHA-1/SHA-256/SHA-512 checksums of files.
  * Upload files of any size, download files, folders and selections as
    ZIP archive, and preview images, PDFs, audio, video and text (other
    files are downloaded).
  * Download files from http:// and https:// URLs into a folder;
    local and private addresses are refused.
  * Compress to ZIP/tar.gz and extract archives, including 7z, RAR and
    ISO images.
  * Disk usage of folders, largest items first.
  * Trash compatible with the Samba recycle bin, with restore, a page
    listing the deleted items of all shared folders and an optional
    automatic cleanup of old items.
  * Share links to files and folders with optional password, expiry and
    download limit, served by a separate, privilege separated server on
    its own port.
  * Audit log in Diagnostics | System Logs.
  * Settings page and optional access for non-administrative users based
    on the shared folder privileges and the file system permissions.

 -- OpenMediaVault Plugin Developers <plugins@omv-extras.org>  Wed, 01 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
